{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 4, :comments ["<b>Words of</b>: connected to what is written above, 'all flesh shall come to You,' for You hear prayer — that You heard my prayer when I confessed my iniquities and [when] You forgave all our transgressions. The poet composed this psalm in a year of drought; they prayed to HaShem and He heard their prayer." "And the meaning of <b>they prevailed over me</b>: the words of the praying poet, for I confessed, for my iniquities were great and I and my people transgressed; therefore the affliction of drought came."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 65, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:32:42.588196018Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}